7. Core Logic as Executable Pseudocode
7.1 Create Philosophical Argument
function createPhilosophicalArgument(argument, files, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Validate the argument against the schema. If invalid, return an error with the details.

Step 3. If the work reference is present, look it up. If null, flag it as unresolved.

Step 4. If the student argument reference is present, look it up. If null, flag it as unresolved.

Step 5. Generate an argument ID. Set the fields: version 1, moderation_status pending, deposit_date now, depositor_id from auth, depositor_affiliation from auth, provenance from provenance.

Step 6. Insert the philosophical argument.

Step 7. Insert the philosopher records, the premise records, the assumption records, the objection records, the response records, the term records, and the argument relations.

Step 8. Insert the work link and the student argument link if present.

Step 9. Insert the provenance.

Step 10. Insert the moderation record.

Step 11. Insert the audit log entry.

Step 12. Return the argument_id and the status created.

7.2 Read Philosophical Argument
function readPhilosophicalArgument(argumentId, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the argument. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Read the philosophers, the premises, the assumptions, the objections, the responses, the terms, the relations, the links, the provenance, and the moderation.

Step 4. Reconstruct the deposit.

Step 5. Insert the audit log entry.

Step 6. Return the deposit.

7.3 Update Philosophical Argument
function updatePhilosophicalArgument(argumentId, argument, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing argument. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Validate the new argument.

Step 4. Increment the version. Update the supersedes and superseded_by fields.

Step 5. Insert a provenance record with operation update.

Step 6. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 7. Return the argument_id, the version, and the status updated.

7.4 Delete Philosophical Argument
function deletePhilosophicalArgument(argumentId, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "admin"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing argument. If null, return an error.

Step 3. If soft delete, mark as deleted. Otherwise, remove.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the argument_id and the status deleted.

